    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about room modes and physical mass, but it's more than just a standing wave. the timing of the vibration is too precise, it's like it's responding to the *intent* of the chord rather than just the amplitude. it's not just about acoustics, it's about the way these specific dissonant intervals interact with the neural bio-electrical field. if we treat the human consciousness as a complex oscillator with its own damping coefficient, wouldn't we be able to model a theoretical frequency that correlates to the \"strength\" of that oscillation? like, if you look at it through the lens of neuro-physics rather than just traditional acoustics, can we at least attempt to approximate a threshold?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
