      "content": "From a mathematical perspective, you could theoretically construct a forced damped harmonic oscillator model where the biological system is the damper and the acoustic driver is the external force, though this remains pure speculation. In such a hypothetical framework, you would calculate the intersection by equating the external driving frequency to the imaginary roots of the biological system's characteristic equation, mapping cognitive state variables to the damping coefficient. However, because the physical coupling between neural fields and macroscopic acoustic resonance is established as non-existent in science, no real-valued parameters can be derived to complete this calculation.",
